"use strict";(self.webpackChunkdatabricks_monolith=self.webpackChunkdatabricks_monolith||[]).push([[67998],{67998:e=>{e.exports='# Data Engineering: Spark Declarative Pipelines\n\nDomain knowledge for building data pipelines with Spark Declarative Pipelines (formerly Delta Live Tables / DLT).\n\n## Decision Tree\n\nUse this tree to determine which dataset type and features to use:\n\n```\nUser request → What kind of output?\n├── Intermediate/reusable logic (not persisted) → Temporary View\n│   ├── Preprocessing/filtering before Auto CDC → Temporary View feeding CDC flow\n│   ├── Shared intermediate streaming logic reused by multiple downstream tables\n│   ├── Pipeline-private helper logic (not published to catalog)\n│   └── Published to UC for external queries → Persistent View (SQL only)\n├── Persisted dataset\n│   ├── Source is streaming/incremental/continuously growing → Streaming Table\n│   │   ├── File ingestion (cloud storage, Volumes) → Auto Loader\n│   │   ├── Message bus (Kafka, Kinesis, Pub/Sub, Pulsar, Event Hubs) → streaming source read\n│   │   ├── CDC / upserts / track changes / keep latest per key / SCD Type 1 or 2 → Auto CDC\n│   │   ├── Multiple sources into one table → Append Flows (NOT union)\n│   │   └── Windowed aggregation with watermark → stateful streaming\n│   └── Source is batch/historical/full scan → Materialized View\n│       ├── Aggregation/join across full dataset (GROUP BY, SUM, COUNT, etc.)\n│       ├── Gold layer aggregation from streaming table → MV with batch read\n│       └── JDBC/Federation/external batch sources\n├── Output to external system (Python only) → Sink\n│   ├── Existing external table → Sink with format="delta"\n│   ├── Kafka / Event Hubs → Sink with format="kafka"\n│   └── Custom merge/upsert logic per batch → ForEachBatch Sink\n└── Data quality constraints → Expectations (on any dataset type)\n```\n\n## Common Traps\n\n- **"Create a table"** without specifying type → ask whether the source is streaming or batch\n- **Materialized View from streaming source** is an error → use a Streaming Table\n- **Streaming Table from batch source** is an error → use a Materialized View\n- **Aggregation over streaming table** → use a Materialized View with batch read, NOT a Streaming Table\n- **Union of streams** → use multiple Append Flows. UNION is an anti-pattern for streaming sources.\n- **Changing dataset type** → cannot change ST→MV or MV→ST without dropping the existing table first\n- **Python-only features**: Sinks, ForEachBatch Sinks, CDC from snapshots, custom data sources\n\n## Auto Loader (cloudFiles)\n\nIncrementally ingest files from cloud storage into Delta Lake tables.\n\n**SQL syntax:**\n\n```sql\nCREATE OR REFRESH STREAMING TABLE my_table\nAS SELECT * FROM STREAM read_files(\n  \'/path/to/files\',\n  format => \'json\',\n  header => true\n);\n```\n\n**Python syntax:**\n\n```python\n@dp.table()\ndef my_table():\n    return (spark.readStream\n        .format("cloudFiles")\n        .option("cloudFiles.format", "json")\n        .option("cloudFiles.inferColumnTypes", "true")\n        .load("/path/to/files"))\n```\n\nSupported formats: JSON, CSV, Parquet, Avro, ORC, XML, Text. Use `schemaHints` to override inferred types.\n\n## Streaming Tables\n\nProcess data continuously with exactly-once semantics.\n\n**SQL:**\n\n```sql\nCREATE OR REFRESH STREAMING TABLE bronze_events\nAS SELECT * FROM STREAM read_files(\'/data/events\', format => \'json\');\n```\n\n**Python:**\n\n```python\n@dp.table()\ndef bronze_events():\n    return spark.readStream.format("cloudFiles").option("cloudFiles.format", "json").load("/data/events")\n```\n\n### Append Flows (fan-in from multiple sources)\n\n```sql\nCREATE OR REFRESH STREAMING TABLE all_events;\n\nCREATE FLOW append_source1 INSERT INTO all_events BY NAME\nAS SELECT * FROM STREAM source1;\n\nCREATE FLOW append_source2 INSERT INTO all_events BY NAME\nAS SELECT * FROM STREAM source2;\n```\n\n## Materialized Views\n\nPhysically store query results, refreshed incrementally.\n\n**SQL:**\n\n```sql\nCREATE OR REFRESH MATERIALIZED VIEW daily_summary\nAS SELECT date, COUNT(*) as total, SUM(amount) as revenue\n   FROM bronze_orders\n   GROUP BY date;\n```\n\n**Python:**\n\n```python\n@dp.materialized_view()\ndef daily_summary():\n    return spark.read.table("bronze_orders").groupBy("date").agg(count("*").alias("total"), sum("amount").alias("revenue"))\n```\n\n## Views\n\n- **Temporary View**: Pipeline-private, not published to UC\n- **Persistent View** (SQL only): Published to Unity Catalog\n\n```sql\nCREATE TEMPORARY VIEW filtered_data AS SELECT * FROM raw_data WHERE valid = true;\nCREATE VIEW catalog.schema.published_view AS SELECT * FROM my_table;\n```\n\n## Auto CDC (Change Data Capture)\n\nProcess CDC feeds handling inserts, updates, and deletes.\n\n**SQL:**\n\n```sql\nCREATE OR REFRESH STREAMING TABLE target_table;\nAUTO CDC INTO target_table\nFROM STREAM source_cdc\nKEYS (id)\nSEQUENCE BY timestamp\nCOLUMNS * EXCEPT (_rescued_data)\nSTORED AS SCD TYPE 1;\n```\n\n**Python:**\n\n```python\ndp.create_streaming_table("target_table")\ndp.create_auto_cdc_flow(\n    target="target_table",\n    source="source_cdc",\n    keys=["id"],\n    sequence_by=col("timestamp"),\n    stored_as_scd_type=1,\n)\n```\n\n## Expectations (Data Quality)\n\nDefine constraints on pipeline datasets:\n\n**SQL:**\n\n```sql\nCREATE OR REFRESH STREAMING TABLE clean_data (\n  CONSTRAINT valid_id EXPECT (id IS NOT NULL) ON VIOLATION DROP ROW,\n  CONSTRAINT valid_amount EXPECT (amount > 0) ON VIOLATION FAIL UPDATE\n) AS SELECT * FROM STREAM raw_data;\n```\n\n**Python:**\n\n```python\n@dp.table()\n@dp.expect_or_drop("valid_id", "id IS NOT NULL")\n@dp.expect_or_fail("valid_amount", "amount > 0")\ndef clean_data():\n    return spark.readStream.table("raw_data")\n```\n\n## How to Work with Pipelines via the Databricks Agent\n\nUse these tools for pipeline operations:\n\n- **Create a pipeline**: `createAsset({ assetType: \'pipeline\', name: \'My Pipeline\' })` then `editAsset` to add pipeline files\n- **View pipeline details**: `runDatabricksCli` with `pipelines get --pipeline-id <id> --output JSON`\n- **Start a pipeline update**: `runDatabricksCli` with `pipelines start-update --pipeline-id <id>`\n- **List pipelines**: `runDatabricksCli` with `pipelines list-pipelines --output JSON`\n- **Create pipeline code**: Use `executeCode` to test SQL/Python snippets, then `createAsset` to persist as a notebook or pipeline file\n- **Navigate to pipeline**: `openAsset({ assetType: \'pipeline\', assetId: \'<id>\' })` with `continueMessage` for the Data Engineer agent\n\n## Import Conventions\n\n| Current                                           | Deprecated                       |\n| ------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------- |\n| `from pyspark import pipelines as dp`             | `import dlt`                     |\n| `spark.read.table()` / `spark.readStream.table()` | `dp.read()` / `dp.read_stream()` |\n| `CREATE OR REFRESH STREAMING TABLE`               | `CREATE STREAMING LIVE TABLE`    |\n| `CREATE OR REFRESH MATERIALIZED VIEW`             | `CREATE LIVE TABLE`              |\n'}}]);
